1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,860
Expand x plus two, to the power
nine, and you get ten long terms.

2
00:00:05,260 --> 00:00:07,522
But the question only wants one of them.

3
00:00:07,522 --> 00:00:08,583
The seventh term.

4
00:00:09,033 --> 00:00:13,152
Diya is about to write out all ten
terms, just to reach number seven.

5
00:00:13,502 --> 00:00:17,558
Is there a way to jump straight to
the seventh term, and skip the other

6
00:00:17,558 --> 00:00:18,458
nine?

7
00:00:18,552 --> 00:00:19,452
There is.

8
00:00:19,288 --> 00:00:21,183
It is called the general term.

9
00:00:21,183 --> 00:00:23,311
One formula for any term you want.

10
00:00:23,961 --> 00:00:26,095
Start with a row of lockers.

11
00:00:26,095 --> 00:00:27,677
Locker one is empty.

12
00:00:27,677 --> 00:00:29,534
Locker two has one coin.

13
00:00:29,534 --> 00:00:31,552
Locker three has two coins.

14
00:00:31,952 --> 00:00:33,010
See the pattern?

15
00:00:33,010 --> 00:00:35,669
Each locker has one coin
less than its number.

16
00:00:36,069 --> 00:00:38,058
So locker seven has six coins.

17
00:00:38,058 --> 00:00:41,810
You do not need to open the
first six lockers to know that.

18
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:44,789
An expansion works the same way.

19
00:00:44,789 --> 00:00:47,467
Look at a plus b, to the power n.

20
00:00:47,867 --> 00:00:50,335
Term one has b to the power zero.

21
00:00:50,335 --> 00:00:52,751
Term two has b to the power one.

22
00:00:52,751 --> 00:00:54,617
Term three has b squared.

23
00:00:55,017 --> 00:00:58,705
So the term in place r plus
one has b to the power r.

24
00:00:58,705 --> 00:01:02,117
Term number is always one
more than the power of b.

25
00:01:02,767 --> 00:01:03,783
Watch it run.

26
00:01:03,783 --> 00:01:07,481
Here are all eleven terms of
a plus b, to the power ten.

27
00:01:07,881 --> 00:01:10,426
Now the pointer walks along the terms.

28
00:01:10,426 --> 00:01:14,120
As the term number goes up
by one, r goes up by one.

29
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,444
At term seven, r is six.

30
00:01:16,444 --> 00:01:21,190
So the seventh term has b to the
power six, and a to the power four.

31
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:25,121
Now let us build the formula
in three small steps.

32
00:01:25,471 --> 00:01:26,371
Step one.

33
00:01:26,256 --> 00:01:29,634
The term in place r plus
one has b to the power r.

34
00:01:29,634 --> 00:01:31,308
That is the locker rule.

35
00:01:32,058 --> 00:01:32,958
Step two.

36
00:01:32,854 --> 00:01:35,212
The two powers always add up to n.

37
00:01:35,212 --> 00:01:37,483
So the power of a is n minus r.

38
00:01:38,233 --> 00:01:39,133
Step three.

39
00:01:39,021 --> 00:01:43,150
The number in front is n C r, the ways
to choose the r brackets that give

40
00:01:43,150 --> 00:01:44,050
b.

41
00:01:44,251 --> 00:01:45,562
Put it together.

42
00:01:45,562 --> 00:01:51,047
T r plus one equals n C r, times a
to the n minus r, times b to the r.

43
00:01:51,047 --> 00:01:52,964
That is the general term.

44
00:01:53,614 --> 00:01:54,657
Side by side.

45
00:01:54,657 --> 00:01:57,447
Many people mix up the term number with r.

46
00:01:57,847 --> 00:01:59,883
The seventh term is T seven.

47
00:01:59,883 --> 00:02:03,925
To write it as T r plus one,
r must be six, not seven.

48
00:02:04,325 --> 00:02:06,427
So always subtract one first.

49
00:02:06,427 --> 00:02:08,917
Term number minus one gives you r.

50
00:02:09,517 --> 00:02:10,497
Now you try.

51
00:02:10,497 --> 00:02:15,132
In a plus b, to the power ten, does
the seventh term have b to the power

52
00:02:15,132 --> 00:02:16,302
six, or seven?

53
00:02:16,302 --> 00:02:17,521
Pause and decide.

54
00:02:20,721 --> 00:02:21,621
Six!

55
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:25,830
The first term has b to the zero, so
the seventh term has b to the six.

56
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:27,623
Remember this.

57
00:02:27,623 --> 00:02:32,848
The term in place r plus one is n C
r, times a to the n minus r, times

58
00:02:32,848 --> 00:02:33,959
b to the r.

59
00:02:34,659 --> 00:02:38,089
The general term can also
hunt down a power of x.

60
00:02:38,439 --> 00:02:41,473
Take x plus one over x, to the power six.

61
00:02:41,473 --> 00:02:43,515
Which term has no x at all?

62
00:02:43,515 --> 00:02:45,801
That is called the constant term.

63
00:02:46,201 --> 00:02:51,613
In the general term, x to the six minus
r, times one over x to the r, gives

64
00:02:51,613 --> 00:02:53,619
x to the six minus two r.

65
00:02:54,369 --> 00:02:56,853
No x means the power is zero.

66
00:02:56,853 --> 00:03:00,487
Six minus two r equals
zero, so r is three.

67
00:03:01,237 --> 00:03:03,976
So the fourth term is the constant term.

68
00:03:03,976 --> 00:03:05,631
Six C three is twenty.

69
00:03:06,281 --> 00:03:07,181
Quick one.

70
00:03:07,138 --> 00:03:11,944
Does x plus one over x, to the power
six, have a term in x to the power

71
00:03:11,944 --> 00:03:12,844
one?

72
00:03:12,446 --> 00:03:13,658
Pause and think.

73
00:03:16,858 --> 00:03:17,758
No!

74
00:03:17,285 --> 00:03:19,256
The power is six minus two r.

75
00:03:19,256 --> 00:03:22,183
That is always even,
so it can never be one.

76
00:03:22,833 --> 00:03:24,523
Now, one worked example.

77
00:03:24,873 --> 00:03:28,319
Find the seventh term of x
plus two, to the power nine.

78
00:03:28,319 --> 00:03:30,167
Diya's question from the start.

79
00:03:30,667 --> 00:03:31,567
Step one.

80
00:03:31,475 --> 00:03:34,115
Seventh term means r plus one is seven.

81
00:03:34,115 --> 00:03:35,188
So r is six.

82
00:03:35,938 --> 00:03:36,838
Step two.

83
00:03:36,783 --> 00:03:37,742
n is nine.

84
00:03:37,742 --> 00:03:42,596
So we need nine C six, times x to
the three, times two to the six.

85
00:03:43,346 --> 00:03:44,248
Step three.

86
00:03:44,248 --> 00:03:46,122
Nine C six is eighty four.

87
00:03:46,122 --> 00:03:48,201
Two to the six is sixty four.

88
00:03:48,951 --> 00:03:53,609
Eighty four times sixty four is five
thousand three hundred seventy six.

89
00:03:53,609 --> 00:03:58,278
So the seventh term is five thousand
three hundred seventy six x cubed.

90
00:03:58,928 --> 00:04:00,389
Now, the exam trap.

91
00:04:00,739 --> 00:04:04,519
Find the fourth term of x
minus two, to the power six.

92
00:04:04,519 --> 00:04:08,659
Many students use b equals two
and get plus one sixty x cubed.

93
00:04:09,059 --> 00:04:11,687
But b is minus two, with the sign.

94
00:04:11,687 --> 00:04:14,242
Minus two, cubed, is minus eight.

95
00:04:14,242 --> 00:04:17,513
So the fourth term is
minus one sixty x cubed.

96
00:04:18,163 --> 00:04:19,479
Where is this asked?

97
00:04:19,479 --> 00:04:23,593
The general term is not in the current
NCERT text, but it is in the JEE

98
00:04:23,593 --> 00:04:24,537
Main syllabus.

99
00:04:24,537 --> 00:04:27,901
JEE Main asks it, for example
to find the constant term.

100
00:04:28,501 --> 00:04:29,724
Exam level now.

101
00:04:29,724 --> 00:04:31,869
Find the term that has no x.

102
00:04:31,869 --> 00:04:33,144
Pause and solve.

103
00:04:38,544 --> 00:04:40,087
The answer is A.

104
00:04:40,087 --> 00:04:40,987
Sixty.

105
00:04:41,316 --> 00:04:46,959
The general term is six C r, times two
x squared to the six minus r, times

106
00:04:46,959 --> 00:04:49,366
minus one over x, to the r.

107
00:04:49,866 --> 00:04:53,216
The power of x is twelve
minus two r, minus r.

108
00:04:53,216 --> 00:04:55,302
That is twelve minus three r.

109
00:04:55,302 --> 00:04:57,610
Set it to zero, so r is four.

110
00:04:58,110 --> 00:04:59,797
Six C four is fifteen.

111
00:04:59,797 --> 00:05:01,321
Two squared is four.

112
00:05:01,321 --> 00:05:03,806
Minus one to the four is plus one.

113
00:05:03,806 --> 00:05:05,801
Fifteen times four is sixty.

114
00:05:06,401 --> 00:05:07,942
Here is your recap.

115
00:05:07,942 --> 00:05:09,526
Screenshot this card.

116
00:05:12,726 --> 00:05:14,912
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

117
00:05:15,312 --> 00:05:16,212
One.

118
00:05:15,815 --> 00:05:18,054
For the tenth term, what is r?

119
00:05:18,954 --> 00:05:19,854
Two.

120
00:05:19,448 --> 00:05:22,954
Write the general term of
a plus b, to the power n.

121
00:05:23,854 --> 00:05:24,754
Three.

122
00:05:24,461 --> 00:05:28,785
Find the constant term of x plus
one over x, to the power four.

123
00:05:29,885 --> 00:05:34,513
Next time: which is bigger, one point
zero one to the power one thousand,

124
00:05:34,513 --> 00:05:35,689
or ten thousand?

125
00:05:35,689 --> 00:05:39,466
The binomial theorem settles
it, along with the middle term.
